**LEN PrEP Delivery Cost Reduction Trajectory — COMPLETE**

All 4 phases written, progress.json marked `done:true`.

### Three Numbers to Remember

1. **$282/DALY** — LEN PrEP at 2027 generic prices ($65/py total) for targeted 3%-incidence populations. Solidly cost-effective by SSA health-sector standards ($500/DALY threshold).

2. **$23/py** — break-even total delivery cost for $100/DALY (GiveWell bar) at 3% incidence. Below even the self-injection floor ($30-35/py). **LEN will not be a GiveWell-class buy.**

3. **$64→$40→$25** — drug price trajectory drives ~80% of CE improvement. Generic entry (2027) is the single biggest event.

### Key Findings
- LEN PrEP is **already cheaper** than oral PrEP at 2026 branded prices ($94-109 vs $100-300/py)
- **Targeting matters 3× more than cost reduction** — deploying to 3% vs 1% incidence populations swings CE more than the entire 2026→2030+ cost trajectory
- CHAI's acceleration value: **$174-580/DALY** attributable, depending on 6-18mo acceleration assumption and attribution share
- Recommended framing: **fund the ACCELERATION**, not the intervention itself. This is a government/GF budget item that CHAI helps make work sooner.

